# Versioned Coding Agent Pack

KILab keeps reusable agent and skill source under `coding-agent-pack/`. Consumer repositories materialize selected files into the native harness directories; they do not read the pack directory directly.

## Use KILab as a submodule

From the target repository:

```bash
git submodule add https://github.com/franciscosuca/KILab.git .kilab-pack
git -C .kilab-pack checkout v1.16.0
git add .gitmodules .kilab-pack
```

Install selected Copilot resources:

```bash
.kilab-pack/coding-agent-pack/scripts/install-pack.sh \
  --target . \
  --harness copilot \
  --agents all \
  --skills all
```

The installer writes only the native Copilot projection:

```text
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/agents/
.github/skills/
```

It does not modify `.github/workflows/` or `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`.

## Update the pinned pack

```bash
git -C .kilab-pack fetch --tags
git -C .kilab-pack checkout v1.17.0
.kilab-pack/coding-agent-pack/scripts/install-pack.sh \
  --target . --harness copilot --agents all --skills all

git diff
```

Commit the updated submodule pointer and generated harness files only after reviewing the diff.

## Clone without a submodule

```bash
git clone https://github.com/franciscosuca/KILab.git "$HOME/coding-agent-pack-source"
"$HOME/coding-agent-pack-source/coding-agent-pack/scripts/install-pack.sh" \
  --target . --harness copilot --agents all --skills all
```

The pack can also install Claude Code and Pi resources. See [`coding-agent-pack/README.md`](../coding-agent-pack/README.md) for scopes, selectors, Pi conversion, and validation.
